description:
Redland City Council (RCC) is seeking tenders from suitably qualified and experienced contractors to deliver the Russell Island Amenities Renewal Project under a Design and Construct contract. The project is located at 22 High Street, Russell Island and is intended to improve public amenities within the Russell Island town centre through the provision of accessible public toilet facilities, supporting wastewater infrastructure and an expanded outdoor community space adjacent to the Russell Island Library.

The Works include, but are not limited to:

•	Design and construction of a new prefabricated public amenities facility;

•	Design and construction of a dedicated onsite sewage treatment system (OSTS) to service the new amenities facility and the existing Russell Island Library;

•	Decommissioning, removal and disposal of the existing library septic tank, absorption trenches and associated wastewater infrastructure;

•	Feasibility assessment and preliminary design of a proposed library deck and associated roof structure;

•	Completion of all investigations, approvals, certifications, testing, commissioning and associated works necessary to deliver a complete and compliant project outcome.

Whitsunday Regional Council (Council) invites suitably experienced and qualified Suppliers to submit a proposal for the management of Lake Proserpine Holiday Park, located at 66 Station Road, Lake Proserpine, Queensland 4800. The park is situated approximately 30km inland from Proserpine via Crystal Brook Road.

The Holiday Park currently includes:

a) 120 unpowered campsites, with a maximum capacity of 600 guests;

b) Three (3) amenity blocks;

c) One (1) kiosk;

d) 12 steel fire pits;

e) One (1) large communal steel fire pit;

f) One (1) watercraft pontoon, usable at higher dam water levels;

g) A recreational non-motorised water sports concession area;

h) A sewage treatment plant; and

i) Six (6) basic accommodation huts, known as Barra Huts, currently under construction.

The six (6) Barra Huts will provide basic accommodation only and will not include bathroom or kitchen facilities. Each hut is intended to be furnished with a bed frame, mattress, bar fridge, air conditioning, fan, and a table and chair on the veranda. Guests will be responsible for providing their own linen. Floor plans and final specifications are not currently available, as the huts remain in the construction and fit-out process.

Whitsunday Regional Council seeks to engage a Contractor to undertake the management services for Lake Proserpine Holiday Park, commencing 1 February 2027, for an initial period of two (2) years, with an option for one (1) additional 12-month extension at Council's discretion.

A tender site briefing has been set for Thursday 12th November 2026, 10.00am at Lake Proserpine Holiday Park, 66 Station Road, Lake Proserpine 4800. Please RSVP via email to contracts@whitsundayrc.qld.gov.au by 12,.00pm on Wednesday 11th November 2026.

